          >. For candidates looking to seek admission into undergraduate
          engineering (B.E/B.Tech) courses, registering correctly and completing
          document verification is mandatory. Any discrepancies in documents
          will result in candidate reassignment to the Open Category. Below is
          the detailed breakdown of guidelines.
        </p>

        <h2 id="scrutiny-mode-en">
          1. Verification Modes: Physical Scrutiny vs. E-Scrutiny
        </h2>
        <p>
          Candidates must choose between the following two modes during the
          application form filling:
        </p>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 my-6">
          <div class="bg-bg-surface border border-border-card p-6 rounded-2xl">
            <h4
              class="text-text-main font-bold mt-0 mb-3 flex items-center gap-2"
            >
              <span class="text-emerald-500">🏢</span> Physical Scrutiny (Highly Recommended)
            </h4>
            <p class="text-sm text-text-muted leading-relaxed mb-0">
              • Book a time slot and visit the nearest facilitation center (FC)
              in person.<br />
              • Verification officers evaluate physical original documents and confirm
              the application instantly.<br />
              • Any registration errors can be edited on-the-spot by the officer.<br
              />
              • <strong
                >Best option for students residing in Maharashtra.</strong
              >
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-bg-surface border border-border-card p-6 rounded-2xl">
            <h4
              class="text-text-main font-bold mt-0 mb-3 flex items-center gap-2"
            >
              <span class="text-amber-500">💻</span> E-Scrutiny (Online Mode)
            </h4>
            <p class="text-sm text-text-muted leading-relaxed mb-0">
              • Upload scanned copies of all required certificates online.<br />
              • Officers review documents remotely from the portal.<br />
              • If documents are unreadable or incorrect, a query is sent back to
              the student's dashboard.<br />
              • Highly time-consuming. Recommended only for candidates residing outside
              Maharashtra (OMS).
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

