        <h2 id="faq-en">5. Common Counselling Problems & Solutions (FAQ)</h2>

        <div class="space-y-4 my-6">
          <div class="bg-bg-surface border border-border-card p-5 rounded-2xl">
            <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-text-main mt-0 mb-2">
              Q: My name spelling differs between Aadhaar Card and 10th
              marksheet. Will my form be rejected?
            </h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-text-muted m-0">
              <strong>Answer:</strong> Minor spelling differences will not lead to
              direct rejection. You must create a notarized affidavit on a **₹500
              stamp paper** explaining the name variance, and show it during Physical
              Scrutiny.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-bg-surface border border-border-card p-5 rounded-2xl">
            <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-text-main mt-0 mb-2">
              Q: I don't have my original Caste Validity certificate yet. What
              should I upload?
            </h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-text-muted m-0">
              <strong>Answer:</strong> You can upload the **acknowledgement receipt**
              of your application for Caste Validity. However, you must present the
              original Caste Validity certificate at the college during final admission.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-bg-surface border border-border-card p-5 rounded-2xl">
            <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-text-main mt-0 mb-2">
              Q: API error occurs when uploading the Caste Validity receipt. How
              to fix?
            </h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-text-muted m-0">
              <strong>Answer:</strong> Log out of the portal, clear your web browser
              cookies/cache, or complete the upload using Google Chrome in Incognito
              mode. If the issue persists, visit a Physical Scrutiny center.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-bg-surface border border-border-card p-5 rounded-2xl">
            <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-text-main mt-0 mb-2">
              Q: Which certificate number should I enter for Caste Validity?
            </h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-text-muted m-0">
              <strong>Answer:</strong> Do not enter the barcode number. Input the
              official **Outward Number (जावक क्रमांक)** printed on the top/bottom
              of your Caste Validity certificate.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-bg-surface border border-border-card p-5 rounded-2xl">
            <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-text-main mt-0 mb-2">
              Q: My mobile number is closed, and I'm not getting the OTP. What
              should I do?
            </h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-text-muted m-0">
              <strong>Answer:</strong> You cannot change it yourself. You must contact
              the CET Cell support via official helpline or send an email requesting
              a mobile number modification.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-bg-surface border border-border-card p-5 rounded-2xl">
            <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-text-main mt-0 mb-2">
              Q: During E-Scrutiny, my category got changed to Open. How do I
              fix this?
            </h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-text-muted m-0">
              <strong>Answer:</strong> Category is converted to Open when submitted
              certificates are invalid or incomplete. Check the query logs in your
              dashboard, correct the documents, re-upload them, or visit the nearest
              FC to restore your category status.
            </p>
          </div>
